<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06PD">Example <span data-tag="06PD">9.5.4.8</span> <span class="named">(Products of Presentable $\infty $-Categories)</span>.</a> Let $\{  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i \} _{i \in I}$ be a small collection of presentable $\infty $-categories. Then the product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}= \prod _{i \in I} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_ i$ is presentable. This can be regarded as a special case of Proposition <a data-tag="06PC" href="/tag/06PC">9.5.4.7</a> (see Example <a data-tag="03EP" href="/tag/03EP">7.6.1.20</a>). Alternatively, it follows from Corollary <a data-tag="06KQ" href="/tag/06KQ">9.4.7.18</a> (which guarantees that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is accessible) and Example <a data-tag="069M" href="/tag/069M">7.1.3.11</a> (which guarantees that it is cocomplete). </p>
